WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.297
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.660
SPEAKER: Cloud data
loss prevention

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.550
is a fully managed
service designed

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.040
to help you discover,
classify, and protect

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.600
your most sensitive data.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.020
You can inspect, mask, an
de-identify sensitive data

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.550
such as personally identifiable
information or PII, secrets,

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.780
and credentials.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.230
Cloud DLP integrates natively
with Security Command Center.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.160
When you use Cloud DLP to scan
your GCP storage repositories,

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.860
it can send results directly
to the Security Command Center

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:32.640
dashboard.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.420
Please note.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.360
Cloud DLP uses its own
pricing structure separate

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.680
from Security Command
Center Premium.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.760
A link to pricing information
is available in the description

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.600
below.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.150
Before you can send
Cloud DLP scan results

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.070
to Security Command
Center, you must set up

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:50.240
the following components--

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.020
identify GCP storage
repositories,

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:57.550
set Cloud IAM roles, enable
Security Command Center,

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:02.290
enable Cloud DLP, enable
Cloud DLP as a security source

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:07.520
for Security Command Center,
and define a DLP inspect job.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.420
Step one.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.870
Identify a GCP
storage repositories.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.600
You can choose whether you want
to scan your own GCP storage

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.030
repository or an example one.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.210
If you want to scan your own
existing cloud storage bucket,

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.270
BigQuery table, or Cloud
Datastore kind, first,

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.830
open the project that
the repository is in.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.030
In the next steps, you'll enable
Cloud DLP for this project

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.230
and its organization.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:31.970
Step two.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:34.250
Set Cloud IAM rules.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:37.520
Before you can use Cloud DLP to
send scan results to Security

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.020
Command Center, you'll need to
enable some Cloud IAM rules.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.300
This section requires you
to have the organization

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.910
administrator IAM role.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.920
Click on the organization
dropdown list

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.720
and select the
organization for what

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.940
you want to enable
Security Command Center.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:57.320
Navigate to IAM and Admin
using the Navigation pane.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.970
Find the user name in the
member column or add a new user.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.900
Add the role, Security Center
Admin and DLP Jobs Editor

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.000
and then click Save.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:13.010
Step three, enable
Security Command Center.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.710
If you are a new user, enable
Security Command Center

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:18.410
following the instructions
in the three-step overview

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.820
video linked below.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.600
Step four.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.540
Enable Cloud DLP.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.920
Navigate to the
project you would

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.770
like to use to
execute your DLP scan.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.050
The project must be within
the same organization

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.810
where you enabled
Security Command Center.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:37.720
Head to APIs and Services
in the Navigation pane.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.810
Search for Cloud DLP,
API, and enable it.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:42.680
Step five.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.020
Enable Cloud DLP as
a security source

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.480
for Security Command Center.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.520
Go to the Security
Command Center page

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.160
and select your organization.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.710
Click Settings in the top
right corner of the page.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.280
Under Integrated Sources,
click the toggle next

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.700
to Data Loss Prevention.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.660
Step six.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.610
Define a DLP inspect job.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:09.920
Go to the Cloud DLP console
and choose your project,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.360
click on Create
Job, enter a name

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.820
and select the storage
target that you want to scan.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.685
Configure your scan options.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.090
On the action step, click to
enable Publish the Security

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.530
Command Center.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.950
You also have the option to
save the results to BigQuery,

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.480
click Create, and run the job.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.930
If you want to surface findings
for additional projects

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.680
within your organization, repeat
step six for each storage asset

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.390
that you went to inspect.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.000
Now, findings for
Cloud DLP will display

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.220
in the Findings tab of the
Security Command Center

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.170
dashboard.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:53.410
Cloud DLP uses information
types or info types

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.360
to define what it scans for.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.730
An info type is a
type of sensitive data

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.970
such as a name, email
address, telephone number,

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.520
identification number, credit
card number, and so on.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.240
You can also define your own
custom info types or tune

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.180
detection using
inspection rules.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:14.470
You can find out more about it
in the Cloud DLP documentation.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.149
In our environment,
we see that there

00:04:16.149 --> 00:04:19.870
have been more than 90 Cloud
DLP findings in our organization

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.810
such as email addresses,
credit card numbers, and phone

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:23.590
numbers.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.590
Drilling in, let's expand
an email address finding.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:29.110
We can see it first
occurred on August 25

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.370
and is located in the asset
we identified for inspect job.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.030
This is the project in
which the PII was flagged.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:39.360
We can then click on
the external URI source

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.240
and see almost 4,000 PII
findings related to it.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.840
Next, if set up as
part of the DLP job,

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.640
we can perform
additional analysis

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.440
on this data their BigQuery.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.380
Or we can remove this resource
and remediate these findings

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.780
by contacting the owner.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.100
Congratulations.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.040
You've enabled Cloud DLP
for Security Command Center

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.070
and learned how to respond
to a finding from it.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:05.420
[MUSIC PLAYING]

